title: 'cumulus: submit V2/V3 collations as segments'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |
    The slot-based collator now submits every collation through
    `CollationGenerationMessage::SubmitSegment`: a V2 collation as a one-element segment
    and a V3 collation as a segment carrying its scheduling proof. This is groundwork for
    candidate resubmission, where a segment carries resubmitted entries ahead of the
    freshly built bundle.

    `SchedulingSignals` moves from `cumulus-pallet-parachain-system` to
    `cumulus-primitives-core` so the collator and the PVF share one implementation. This
    is a breaking change for `cumulus-pallet-parachain-system`: the type is no longer
    reachable under `validate_block::scheduling`. On a resubmission the collator rebuilds the
    candidate's UMP scheduling tail from the signed scheduling info with the same code the
    PVF applies, so receipt commitments cannot drift from the PVF's output.
crates:
- name: cumulus-client-consensus-aura
  bump: patch
- name: cumulus-primitives-core
  bump: minor
- name: cumulus-pallet-parachain-system
  bump: major
- name: cumulus-client-collator
  bump: patch
